Optional KV-cache group size for hybrid (full + sliding-window) layouts,
set with VLLM_KV_CACHE_GROUP_SIZE; unset keeps vLLM's heuristic.

Apertus 1.5 8B (32 full-attention layers) with the DSpark drafter (5
sliding-window layers) gets groups of 5: the target's 32 layers are padded to
35 slots, about 9% more KV per token than the target needs. Smaller groups
remove the padding at the cost of more block tables per request.

--- a/workspace/vllm/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py
+++ b/workspace/vllm/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py
@@ -1226,6 +1226,14 @@
         # layers while accommodating speculative decoding drafters that add
         # extra layers to one attention type.
         group_size = max_num_layers
+    override = os.environ.get("VLLM_KV_CACHE_GROUP_SIZE")
+    if override:
+        # Apertus 8B + DSpark is 32 full + 5 sliding-window layers: the
+        # heuristic picks groups of 5 and pads the full layers to 35 (9% of
+        # the target's KV). Groups of 1 (or 2, 4) avoid that at the cost of
+        # more block tables.
+        group_size = int(override)
+        logger.info("KV cache group size %d (VLLM_KV_CACHE_GROUP_SIZE)", group_size)
     grouped_layers = []
     for layers in same_type_layers.values():
         num_padding_layers = group_size - len(layers) % group_size
